		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=32053#p32053"><![CDATA[
Are you using existing constraints, that are solved together (by PhysX) or are you manually applying external forces? Multiple constraints shouldn't cancel eachother.<br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>How do physics engines solve the constraint of multiple objects?</div></blockquote>Pairwise constraints should work fine, as long as they are solved together. Another way is using multi body joints, such as Featherstone. That's what we added to Bullet recently.<br><br>Thanks,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Thu Oct 31, 2013 5:17 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
